From abdaaa8be5c538491e35732b9e64080cd9c5f48a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:03:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(amiga): add Network page with Wi-Fi status and network
 join

New Network tab shows the FujiNet's Wi-Fi link state, saved SSID, signal,
access point, IP/subnet/gateway/DNS, station MAC and firmware version
(Refresh re-reads). Join... scans (paged, up to 32 networks), lists name,
signal and Open/Secured with the saved or strongest network selected, takes
a passphrase in the Pass field and saves SSID + passphrase on the FujiNet
(persist + reconnect, pinned BSSID cleared), then waits up to 10 s and
reports connected / failed / still connecting. Rejoining the saved network
with an empty Pass keeps its stored passphrase; the field and its undo
copy are wiped when leaving the picker. MAC and firmware need firmware with
Wi-Fi GET_ADAPTER_INFO and otherwise read "Needs newer firmware".

SCRIPT gains wifi status|scan|connect N [pass]|join SSID [pass]|cancel,
page network and dump network. Built-in help gets a Network and Wi-Fi topic;
docs/amiga-config.md documents the page and commands.

Verification: make test-amiga-host (1035 checks, 0 failures; new test_net
and test_ctl_net against an in-memory Wi-Fi fake with paged scans);
make amiga AMIGA_PROFILE=wb13|wb31|wb32 (0 warnings); end-to-end SCRIPT
run of the controller linked with the linux fujinet-nio-lib against the
POSIX fujinet-nio firmware (simulated Wi-Fi): status, MAC, firmware, scan,
connect and join persisted to fujinet.yaml. Amiberry guest not run: no
Kickstart ROM in this environment.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WnuNydgtRyXCoECm974X7F
